        "original_id": "db9fc852-8213-51e6-b56d-be82d0569695",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Organizations: Navy Region Hawaii, Pacific Missile Range Facility\n- Places: Kekaha, Kauai County, Hawaii\n- Systems: Pacific Missile Range Facility Barking Sands airport codes\n- Concepts: Installation support, missile testing and training ranges\n\nFacts:\n- Navy Region Hawaii oversees installation support for the Pacific Missile Range Facility in Kekaha, Hawaii.\n- The Pacific Missile Range Facility is described as the world's largest instrumented, multi-dimensional testing and training missile range.\n- The Pacific Missile Range Facility, Barking Sands is a U.S. naval facility and airport located five nautical miles northwest of Kekaha's central business district in Kauai County, Hawaii, United States.\n- The Pacific Missile Range Facility, Barking Sands has the airport codes IATA BKH, ICAO PHBK, and FAA LID BKH.",
